WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:03.970 line:0%
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Nicolle Wallace.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.271 line:0%
Nicolle, today was harrowing
and terrifying.

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:07.307
In an effort to
lighten things up a little bit,

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:11.344
there is a great new development
in television,

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:17.950
which is my dear friend Leslie
Jones has started watching MSNBC

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.886
and basically live-tweeting it

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:22.054
for what seems like
multiple hours a day.

00:00:22.054 --> 00:00:23.723
Are you aware of this?

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.124
-I am a groupie.

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:28.561
I mean, I'm like whatever
10 steps past a fan is.

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.830
And we love her
so much in my house

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.966
that my son
watches some of them.

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:35.101
We do earmuffs
for the bad language.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.704
-Bet you got to do a lot of
earmuffs when it's Leslie Jones.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:41.607
-When he put my glasses on,
my son now talks like Leslie.

00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:43.809
You know, "Nikki putting
her glasses on!" you know.

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:45.612
We love her. We love her.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.379
-Yeah. Just for those
who haven't seen,

00:00:47.379 --> 00:00:50.449
here's a quick clip
of how Leslie reacts

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:53.619
when she's watching Nicolle
on MSNBC.

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:55.688
-Yas, Nicolle!

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:56.856
Yas, Joy!

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:59.258
Y'all look good with your pink
and your purple!

00:00:59.258 --> 00:01:01.427
Look at Joy! Beautiful smile!

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:02.728
Look at Nicolle!

00:01:02.728 --> 00:01:05.364
Where your glasses at, Nicolle?
We gon' need them.

00:01:05.364 --> 00:01:07.000
-She mentioned the glasses
right there.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.402
She very much likes the Nicolle
move of putting the glasses on.

00:01:10.402 --> 00:01:13.072
-Well, I'm blind as a bat,
so I think --

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:17.143
Tucker Carlson once made fun
of me for doing it for show,

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.711
but I wish that were the case.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.946
I'm blind as a bat,
so I can't read a thing.

00:01:20.946 --> 00:01:24.683
-Gotcha. So, what presents
as you're about to get serious

00:01:24.683 --> 00:01:27.520
is in reality, you have to
put them on to read.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:28.821
-Well, and you'll appreciate

00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:30.590
that sometimes it's
I have no idea what's next,

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:32.658
so I put on my glasses
to see, you know...

00:01:32.658 --> 00:01:33.959
-Right, of course. Yeah.

00:01:33.959 --> 00:01:35.528
-...what I'm supposed
to be doing.

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.930
-I have been there, as well.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:40.566
Hey, I want to talk
about last night.

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:43.369
You know, we did have
this election result.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:46.105
And, you know,
we had two candidates

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:51.210
that, you know, were I guess
endorsed by the president,

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.513
though it seemed like
he was putting more energy

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:56.915
in talking about himself than
he was in talking about them.

00:01:56.915 --> 00:01:58.484
What was your takeaway

00:01:58.484 --> 00:02:03.489
insofar as how Trump affected
last night's results?

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:05.258
-Look, I think
what happened last night

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:08.494
is very much connected
to what happened today

00:02:08.494 --> 00:02:09.995
in good and bad ways.

00:02:09.995 --> 00:02:14.934
I mean, President-Elect Biden
and his new attorney general --

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.902
We learned today
who that's going to be.

00:02:16.902 --> 00:02:18.271
It's going to be
Merrick Garland,

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:21.174
who President Obama had
nominated to the Supreme Court

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:23.142
and Mitch McConnell blocked.

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:26.779
They're going to
have to really look

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:28.781
at investigating the president

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:31.450
and investigating his supporters
and people that were there.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:35.387
And that's just one department.
That's DOJ.

00:02:35.387 --> 00:02:37.756
The Biden agenda, they --

00:02:37.756 --> 00:02:41.393
I talked to a person in
the incoming Biden White House,

00:02:41.393 --> 00:02:44.263
and she said to me, "We don't
know what we don't know."

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:46.766
I think it is so important

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:49.769
that Biden can move at lightning
speed in the beginning

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:51.504
to get vaccines into our arms.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:54.339
I mean, we haven't even
mentioned it yet,

00:02:54.339 --> 00:02:58.277
but I think almost 4,000 people
died today of COVID.

00:02:58.277 --> 00:03:00.380
So President-Elect Biden
has his hands full.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:03.583
And it is a really,
really, really good thing

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:04.850
that he's going to have control,

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:06.719
his party controlling
the Senate,

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:10.356
so that he can get, at least
for the first two years,

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:12.658
as much of his agenda
through as possible.

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:16.429
-Do you think
that historians will look back

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:20.833
on the way the president
involved himself in this race

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:25.237
and frame it as maybe
one of the worst strategies?

00:03:25.237 --> 00:03:26.739
-I hope it's something bigger.

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:28.774
I mean, I hope it goes back to
what you said in the beginning,

00:03:28.774 --> 00:03:31.811
and I hope that we can add
voters rejecting.

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:36.215
I mean, Kelly Loeffler and David
Perdue were coup enthusiasts.

00:03:36.215 --> 00:03:41.086
They were for overturning the
results of November's election.

00:03:41.086 --> 00:03:46.826
And I think that if you can take
any sort of solace

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:48.894
in some of what we've seen,

00:03:48.894 --> 00:03:51.764
is that in November, Donald
Trump was roundly rejected,

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:53.632
and in Georgia, his allies,

00:03:53.632 --> 00:03:56.068
who had wrapped themselves
around him --

00:03:56.068 --> 00:03:57.670
He was at war

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:01.174
with their own Republican
statewide elected officials.

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:04.076
All of the statewide electeds
in Georgia are Republicans.

00:04:04.076 --> 00:04:06.212
Secretary of State
Raffensperger,

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:09.015
Governor Kemp, Gabe Sterling,
these people who,

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:12.518
in comparison to all of
the Republicans in Washington

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:15.120
look like truth-tellers
and heroes, were actually,

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:18.057
until Trump started fighting
his election loss,

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:21.227
likely allies
of Perdue and Kelly.

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:24.797
So it's a good thing
for the country

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:26.999
that Georgia rejected them.

00:04:26.999 --> 00:04:30.636
We'll see if Democrats
can continue that streak.

00:04:30.636 --> 00:04:32.805
But I think
if we can extrapolate

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:37.109
that Reverend Warnock and Jon
Ossoff were superb candidates

00:04:37.109 --> 00:04:40.446
who ran very
disciplined campaigns

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:42.915
during a time
of incredible turmoil --

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:45.217
President-Elect Biden
went to the state and campaigned

00:04:45.217 --> 00:04:48.287
and kept the message very
forward-looking, very positive.

00:04:48.287 --> 00:04:51.757
And it's good
that Georgians selected that.

00:04:51.757 --> 00:04:54.360
But I think that it is --

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.662
It would be unfair
to sort of understate

00:04:56.662 --> 00:04:59.565
just how challenging
the governing climate will be

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:02.468
for Joe Biden and Democrats
in the Congress.

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:04.403
-I do want to swing back
to something you said

00:05:04.403 --> 00:05:07.239
about the elected officials
in Georgia,

00:05:07.239 --> 00:05:10.809
Raffensperger,
Sterling, and Kemp,

00:05:10.809 --> 00:05:15.080
who have defended
time and time again

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:19.352
the authenticity
and, you know, the effectiveness

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:22.221
of the electoral process
in Georgia,

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:24.990
and the very fact
that the Republicans

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:26.325
and the Republican Party

00:05:26.325 --> 00:05:29.062
would certainly espouse
the idea of states' rights.

00:05:29.062 --> 00:05:31.731
And yet you have,
not to go back to it,

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:35.034
but you have, you know, Senator
Hawley today who's from Missouri

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:39.171
talking about how Pennsylvania
should run their elections.

00:05:39.171 --> 00:05:43.208
Does that sort of speak to, you
know, how little meat there is

00:05:43.208 --> 00:05:45.444
on the bones
of what they're criticizing,

00:05:45.444 --> 00:05:47.980
when the states that are, again,
Republican-run states

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.850
are saying, "Hey, guys, we're
the ones on the ground here.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.585
We're also upset
with the results,

00:05:52.585 --> 00:05:56.155
but we can promise you
this has been fair and square"?

00:05:56.155 --> 00:05:57.356
-Yeah, look,
I mean, it's worse --

00:05:57.356 --> 00:05:58.691
It's more egregious than that.

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:00.259
And it means there's no marrow

00:06:00.259 --> 00:06:02.895
inside the bones
of today's Republican Party.

00:06:02.895 --> 00:06:05.331
They're soulless.
They're without principle.

00:06:05.331 --> 00:06:08.234
Their ambition has blinded them
from any --

00:06:08.234 --> 00:06:10.602
Think about
what they strive to do.

00:06:10.602 --> 00:06:11.970
Their ambition means

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:14.172
they want to be the next
president of this country,

00:06:14.172 --> 00:06:15.774
a country
that they don't respect

00:06:15.774 --> 00:06:17.844
or hold in high enough regard

00:06:17.844 --> 00:06:20.112
to honor a choice
that this country made

00:06:20.112 --> 00:06:21.446
in a democratic election.

00:06:21.446 --> 00:06:24.784
So I think that they have been
revealed in Washington

00:06:24.784 --> 00:06:28.087
by some of these statewide
Republican officials who were --

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:30.590
I mean, Georgia's
Republican governor

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:32.524
is as Trumpy as you can get.

00:06:32.524 --> 00:06:36.929
He was in a fight with
Atlanta Mayor Bottoms for months

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:38.230
about mask-wearing.

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:40.499
I mean, these were not
"squishy" Republicans.

00:06:40.499 --> 00:06:42.768
These were Georgia Republicans.

00:06:42.768 --> 00:06:45.404
And to see Josh Hawley,

00:06:45.404 --> 00:06:49.841
the Ivy League-educated Josh
Hawley, trying to undermine

00:06:49.841 --> 00:06:53.779
other Democratic and Republican
statewide officials

00:06:53.779 --> 00:06:56.882
just shows how hollow and craven

00:06:56.882 --> 00:07:01.587
and how sort of driven
by political ambition he is.

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:03.856
And it's sad that we're even
talking about him,

00:07:03.856 --> 00:07:05.358
but he deserves
a lot of the blame

00:07:05.358 --> 00:07:08.327
for what happened
in Congress today.

00:07:08.327 --> 00:07:10.362
-Once again, I really do
want to thank you,

00:07:10.362 --> 00:07:13.900
after basically what I think
is about 24 hours on television,

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:16.435
that you found
an extra 15 minutes for us.

00:07:16.435 --> 00:07:18.704
Thanks so much, Nicolle.
-It's an honor. Thank you.

